  m_text: '<size=150%><b>Welcome to Bird Cafe!</b></size>



    In this game, you
    aren''t just a pet owner... you are a <color=#00AA00><b>Bird Boss</b></color>!
    You''ll manage a cafe where your birds work, play, and live. But remember: being
    a boss means taking care of your team.



    Here is your official guide to
    becoming the best Bird Boss in town!



    <line-height=1.5em>

    <size=120%><b>1.
    Make it Yours!</b></size>

    The first thing you''ll do is <b>Customization</b>.

    *
    <b>Name your bird:</b> Will it be <i>Sir Flaps-a-Lot</i> or <i>DJ Tweety</i>?

    *
    <b>Choose your type:</b> Different birds have different personalities. Some are
    energetic, while others are super chill. Pick the one that fits your style!



    <size=120%><b>2.
    The Daily To-Do List (Pet Care)</b></size>

    To keep your bird happy, you
    need to use your <b>Care Features</b> every day:

    * <b>Feed:</b> Keeps them
    full and energetic.

    * <b>Play:</b> Boosts their mood and keeps them from
    getting "Sad."

    * <b>Rest:</b> Working in a cafe is tiring! Make sure they
    sleep so they stay "Energetic."

    * <b>Health Check:</b> Use the <b>Vet</b>
    to make sure your bird isn''t "Sick."



    <b>Watch for Reactions!</b> Your
    bird will show you how it feels. If it''s sparkling and chirping, you''re doing
    great. If it looks droopy, check its stats!



    <size=120%><b>3. The "Cost
    of Care" (The Real Talk)</b></size>

    Owning a pet is a blast, but it also
    costs <b><color=#00AA00>In-Game Currency</color></b>. Just like in real life,
    you have to budget for:

    * <b>Grocery Bills:</b> Birdseed isn''t free!

    *
    <b>Doctor Visits:</b> Vet bills can be expensive. If you don''t save up, you
    might not be able to help your bird when it gets sick.

    * <b>Fun Stuff:</b>
    Toys make them happy, but do you have enough left for food?



    <b>The Report
    Card:</b> At the end of each week, the game will generate a <b>Presentable Report</b>.
    This shows exactly how much you spent on food vs. fun. A great Bird Boss keeps
    their expenses lower than their earnings!



    <size=120%><b>4. Pro-Strategy:
    How to Win</b></size>



    <b>Strategy #1: The "Emergency Fund"</b>

    Always
    keep a little extra currency in the bank. If your bird gets sick suddenly, a
    Vet visit costs more than a bag of seeds. If you spend all your money on toys,
    you might run out when it matters most!



    <b>Strategy #2: Balance the "Vibe"</b>

    If
    your bird is "Sad," they won''t work well in the cafe, and you''ll earn less
    money. Sometimes, spending a little on a toy today helps you earn much more tomorrow.



    <b>Strategy
    #3: Check the Data</b>

    Use the <b>Summary Screen</b> to see if you are overspending.
    If your "Care Expenses" are too high, try to find cheaper ways to keep your bird
    happy, like extra rest instead of expensive treats.



    <size=120%><b>5. Why
    are we doing this?</b></size>

    Being a pet owner is a mix of <b>Fun</b> and
    <b>Responsibility</b>:



    * <b>The Fun:</b> You get a loyal friend who grows
    with you, learns tricks, and makes you smile.

    * <b>The Responsibility:</b>
    Your bird depends <i>entirely</i> on you. They can''t buy their own food or drive
    to the doctor. Financial responsibility means making sure your pet has what they
    <b>need</b> (Health and Food) before you give them everything they <b>want</b>
    (Toys and Treats).



    <size=130%><color=#00AA00><b>Are you ready to open
    the Cafe? Let''s get flapping!</b></color></size>'
