  m_text: "<size=140%><b>Bird Cafe \u2014 Credits</b></size>\r\n\r\n<b>Project Title</b> 
    \r\nBird Cafe\r\n\r\n<b>Developers</b>  \r\nMorgan Kindle  \r\nKevin Olalia 
    \r\nJoshua Tanczos  \r\n\r\n<b>Project Topic</b>  \r\nVirtual Pet Simulation 
    \r\n<i>(FBLA Introduction to Programming 2025\u20132026)</i>\r\n\r\n<b>Platform</b> 
    \r\n\u2022 Unity 2022.3 LTS \u2014 Game UI and presentation  \r\n\u2022 C# /
    .NET Standard 2.1 \u2014 Shared simulation engine  \r\n\u2022 .NET 6 \u2014 Console
    verification build and automated tests  \r\n\r\n<b>Project Description</b>  \r\nBird
    Cafe is a virtual pet and cafe management simulation where players care for bird
    \u201Cemployees\u201D while operating a small cafe.  \r\nThe game emphasizes
    balancing animal well-being with business performance by tracking care costs,
    revenue, inventory, and profitability through a repeatable daily simulation loop.\r\n\r\n<b>Unity
    UI / Asset Packages</b>  \r\n\u2022 Cute Kawaii GUI Pack \u2014 <i>Ricimi (Unity
    Asset Store)</i>  \r\n\u2022 Easy Tooltip \u2014 <i>Ahmed Benlakhdhar</i>  \r\n\r\nAll
    third-party assets are used in accordance with their respective licenses.\r\n\r\n<b>AI-Assisted
    Development Disclosure</b>  \r\nAI tools were used to assist with early drafts,
    boilerplate generation, and refactoring support.  \r\nAll generated content was
    reviewed, modified, and fully integrated by the developers.\r\n\r\n<b>Tools Referenced</b> 
    \r\n\u2022 ChatGPT  \r\n\u2022 Google Gemini  \r\n\r\n<b>Libraries & Tools</b> 
    \r\n\u2022 Unity 2022.3 LTS  \r\n\u2022 .NET SDK (6+)  \r\n\u2022 NUnit Testing
    Framework  \r\n\r\n<b>License</b>  \r\nThis project is released under the <b>MIT
    License</b>.  \r\nSee the <i>LICENSE</i> file in the repository for full terms.\r\n\r\n<b>Copyright</b> 
    \r\n\xA9 2025\u20132026 Bird Cafe Development Team  \r\nAll original code and
    assets not otherwise attributed are the intellectual property of the developers
    and are distributed under the MIT License.\r\n"
